    {
        "content": "<p>kestred opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15266\">issue #15266</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h3><code>.clif</code> Test Case</h3>\n<p>A function with N loops in a row. Each loop adds its counter to a sum until the counter reaches the second argument,<br>\nthen stores the sum and starts the next loop. It is written as an <code>optimize</code> filetest, so that <code>clif-util test</code> runs<br>\nthe egraph pass alone. Here N = 2:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimize</span>\n<span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opt_level</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">speed</span>\n<span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">loops</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"n\">block0</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iconst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iconst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">jump</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block1</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">block1</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v4</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v5</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">v6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">icmp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ult</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">brif</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block1</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v6</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block2</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">block2</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">store</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v6</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">jump</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block3</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">block3</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v9</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v10</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">v11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v9</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">icmp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ult</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v12</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">brif</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v13</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block3</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v12</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v11</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block4</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">block4</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">store</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v11</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">16</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">jump</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">block5</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">block5</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v14</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v15</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">return</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>gen.sh</code> writes the same test at any N:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"ch\">#!/bin/sh</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># Writes a test of the egraph pass on N loops in a row, each summing its counter until the counter reaches n and</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># storing the sum at p + 8 * i.</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">n</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nv\">1</span><span class=\"k\">:-</span><span class=\"nv\">4</span><span class=\"si\">}</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">printf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'test optimize\\nset opt_level=speed\\ntarget aarch64\\n\\nfunction %%loops(i64, i64) {\\nblock0(v0: i64, v1: i64):\\n    v2 = iconst.i64 0\\n    v3 = iconst.i64 1\\n    jump block1(v2, v2)\\n'</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">$i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>-le<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">$n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nb\">printf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'\\nblock%d(v%d: i64, v%d: i64):\\n    v%d = iadd v%d, v%d\\n    v%d = iadd v%d, v3\\n    v%d = icmp ult v%d, v1\\n    brif v%d, block%d(v%d, v%d), block%d\\n\\nblock%d:\\n    store v%d, v0+%d\\n    jump block%d(v2, v2)\\n'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">$v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">$v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">3</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">$v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">4</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">3</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">4</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">3</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"nv\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span>\n<span class=\"k\">done</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">printf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'\\nblock%d(v%d: i64, v%d: i64):\\n    return\\n}\\n'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">4</span><span class=\"k\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">$((</span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"k\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h3>Steps to Reproduce</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>First, build <code>clif-util</code> from wasmtime v50.0.0, the release that ships cranelift-codegen 0.137.0:<br>\n<code>\n  curl -L https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/archive/refs/tags/v50.0.0.tar.gz | tar xz\n  cd wasmtime-50.0.0\n  cargo build --release -p cranelift-tools --bin clif-util\n  </code></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Then, run the test at four sizes, printing the pass timings with <code>-T</code>, and the instructions retired and peak memory<br>\n  of the whole <code>clif-util</code> process with macOS's <code>/usr/bin/time -l</code>:<br>\n<code>\n  for n in 2048 4096 8192 16384; do\n    sh gen.sh $n &gt; loops.clif\n    echo \"N=$n\"\n    /usr/bin/time -l target/release/clif-util test -T loops.clif 2&gt;&amp;1 |\n      grep -E 'Egraph|instructions retired|maximum resident'\n  done\n  </code></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Then, apply the patch under Extra Info, build again, and run the same loop.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Stock 0.137.0 printed:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">2048</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.013</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.010</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">16334848</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"mi\">560108476</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">4096</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.025</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.021</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">25624576</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"mi\">1213169521</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">8192</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.086</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.078</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">42975232</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"mi\">3108413903</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">16384</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.302</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.287</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">72073216</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"mi\">9081268638</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With the patch:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">2048</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.008</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.006</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">17416192</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"mi\">471986712</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">4096</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.010</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.006</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">25182208</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"mi\">856319878</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">8192</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.022</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.014</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">42795008</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"mi\">1682183177</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n<span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">16384</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mf\">0.046</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mf\">0.031</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Egraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">based</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optimizations</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"mi\">73809920</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">maximum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">resident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"mi\">3338495358</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">instructions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">retired</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The patch leaves the output unchanged. <code>clif-util compile --target aarch64 --set opt_level=speed -p -D</code> printed<br>\nidentical IR and disassembly with and without it at N = 1, 2, 16, 1,024 and 4,096, and <code>clif-util test</code> passed every<br>\nfiletest in <code>cranelift/filetests/filetests</code> with it.</p>\n<h3>Expected Results</h3>\n<p>Compile time grows linearly with N. With the patch, the instructions retired by <code>clif-util</code> nearly double with each<br>\ndoubling of N, and at N = 16,384 the egraph pass takes 0.046 s:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">N</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Egraph pass</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Instructions retired</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Peak memory</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,048</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.008 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.47G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">17 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4,096</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.010 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.86G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">24 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8,192</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.022 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.68G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">41 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">16,384</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.046 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.34G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">70 MB</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Actual Results</h3>\n<p>Compile time grows quadratically with N: at N = 16,384 the egraph pass takes 0.30 s, and with the patch 0.046 s. The<br>\ninstructions retired by <code>clif-util</code> grow 2.2, 2.6 and 2.9 times per doubling of N, and those beyond the patched run's<br>\ngrow 4.0 times, while peak memory does not quite double:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">N</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Egraph pass</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Instructions retired</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Peak memory</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,048</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.013 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.56G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">16 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4,096</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.025 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1.21G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">24 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8,192</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.086 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3.11G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">41 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">16,384</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.302 s</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">9.08G</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">69 MB</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The pass times are the first column of <code>-T</code>. The instructions retired include parsing and verification. Each figure is<br>\nfrom one run, on a machine whose load average was about 47 at the time.</p>\n<h3>Versions and Environment</h3>\n<p>Cranelift version or commit: cranelift-codegen 0.137.0, with regalloc2 0.15.2, built into <code>clif-util</code> from wasmtime<br>\nv50.0.0 (commit ebe5e8df1f4e12c5fc2f5954926881d8d61367d8) with rustc 1.98.0, <code>--release</code> and default features.</p>\n<p>Operating system: macOS 26.6.2 (build 25G83).</p>\n<p>Architecture: arm64 (Apple M5 Pro), compiling for <code>--target aarch64</code>.</p>\n<h3>Extra Info</h3>\n<p>When elaboration places a pure instruction, it looks for the outermost loop that the instruction can be hoisted out<br>\nof. For each argument, it scans <code>loop_stack[..active_loop_depth]</code> from the outside in, for the first loop whose hoist<br>\nblock is dominated by the block where the argument is available. An argument computed inside the current loop, such<br>\nas a counter or a sum, is not available at any hoist block, so the scan reads the whole slice.</p>\n<p>The slice is not only the loops that contain the current block. A loop is popped from <code>loop_stack</code> when the walk of<br>\nthe dominator tree leaves its header's subtree, and in the test case every block after a loop is in that subtree, so<br>\nevery earlier loop in the row stays on the stack. <code>find_active_loop_depth</code> returns the position just past the<br>\ninnermost loop on the stack that contains the block, so the slice includes every earlier sibling too. In the k-th loop<br>\nof the test case the slice has k entries, and the scan reads all of them for every argument computed in the loop.</p>\n<p>A profile of stock <code>clif-util test</code> at N = 32,768 shows 516 of the egraph pass's 531 samples in this scan, a loop of<br>\n<code>DominatorTree::block_dominates</code> calls over the stack's entries.</p>\n<p>The patch finds the same level by a binary search. Each loop header on the stack is dominated by the one before it,<br>\nso each hoist block strictly dominates the next. A value available at one hoist block is therefore available at<br>\nevery later one, and the predicate of the scan is false for a prefix of the stack and true for the rest.<br>\n<code>partition_point</code> returns the first entry where it is true, and the length of the slice where it never is, as the<br>\nscan's <code>unwrap_or(active_loop_depth)</code> did.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Diff\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"gd\">--- a/cranelift/codegen/src/egraph/elaborate.rs</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+++ b/cranelift/codegen/src/egraph/elaborate.rs</span>\n<span class=\"gu\">@@ -627,13 +627,19 @@ impl&lt;'a&gt; Elaborator&lt;'a&gt; {</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                            // hoist-block this value is already\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                            // available at. This is the loop-nest\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                            // level whose hoist-block we hoist to.\n<span class=\"gd\">-                            let hoist_level = self.loop_stack[..active_loop_depth]</span>\n<span class=\"gd\">-                                .iter()</span>\n<span class=\"gd\">-                                .position(|loop_entry| {</span>\n<span class=\"gd\">-                                    self.domtree</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            //</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            // Each hoist-block on the stack dominates the next,</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            // so once the value is available at one, it is</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            // available at all later ones. That lets a binary</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            // search find the level in log time, even when</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            // many loops in a row are on the stack.</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            let hoist_level = self.loop_stack[..active_loop_depth].partition_point(</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                                |loop_entry| {</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                                    !self</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                                        .domtree</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                                        .block_dominates(value.in_block, loop_entry.hoist_block)\n<span class=\"gd\">-                                })</span>\n<span class=\"gd\">-                                .unwrap_or(active_loop_depth);</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                                },</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+                            );</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                            trace!(\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                                \" -&gt; arg: elab_value {:?} hoist level {:?}\",\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>                                value, hoist_level\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>",
